*.pyc
__pycache__/
# coverage.py's data file. It was TRACKED, in a public repository, and it is a
# SQLite database whose `file` table holds the ABSOLUTE PATH of every measured
# source file -- so on the operator's own machine it publishes their username
# and home directory layout, and it dates the run. Untracked and ignored.
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
tests/dashboard_data.json
tests/status.json
tests/dashboard.html

# Runtime artifacts. These carry live operational data -- the integrity chain
# logs MAC addresses and per-run traces; the TX/plan files carry deposit
# addresses, memos, XMR destinations and subaddress indices. Committing any of
# them would publish exactly what this toolchain exists to keep private.
#
# Kept in lockstep with paranoia_mode.wipe_gs_artifacts file/dir patterns:
# anything worth secure-deleting is worth gitignoring. If you add a pattern
# there, add it here too, and vice-versa. An earlier version of this list used
# narrower patterns (e.g. exitplan_v1.json alone, thor_pairs_batch.json*) and
# would have leaked any operator-renamed output.
integrity_chain.log
integrity.log
unsigned_*.json
signed_manifest_v1.json
unsigned_manifest.json
signer_progress.json
broadcast_progress.json
wallet_*.json
# Both shapes: 'thor_pairs_*.json' needs an underscore after 'pairs', so it
# never matched the plain 'thor_pairs.json' the console writes by default.
thor_pairs.json
thor_pairs.json.gpg
thor_pairs_*.json
thor_pairs_*.json.gpg
exitplan_*.json
*.unsigned
*.signed
*.blob
*.wallet
*.wallet.keys
*.wallet.address.txt
.ghostspiral.lock
# integrity_log's serialisation lock
*.log.lock
# Partial writes from atomic_write_json/_text: same plaintext as the final
# file, but no '*.json' pattern matches a '.json.tmp' suffix.
*.json.tmp
*.tmp
# monero-wallet-cli's own staging names, and the signer's scratch dir. The
# signed_monero_tx file is a fully signed, relayable transaction.
unsigned_monero_tx
signed_monero_tx
gs_sign_*/
gs_impout_*/
# Monero's own logs. Clean at the default level, but monero-wallet-cli.log
# carries the full wallet address at --log-level 2, and monerod's log is
# created world-readable (0644).
monero-wallet-cli.log
monero-wallet-rpc.log
monerod.log
bitmonero.log
unsigned/
signed_blobs/
tx_staging/
.venv/

# WAKE AND DELIVERY KEYFILES. Not artifacts -- paranoia_mode deliberately does
# NOT sweep these, because wiping the operator's only delivery key destroys
# every future slip and a wake pairing is a two-box ceremony to rebuild. So
# they are here on their own footing rather than by the lockstep rule above.
#
# The reason they need an entry at all: gs_delivery_key's --out defaults to a
# BARE RELATIVE NAME, so an operator who runs it from a checkout writes a
# sealed X25519 secret into the working tree. It is Argon2id-sealed, which is
# not a reason to publish it.
gs_delivery.key
gs_wake_*.key
*.key

# The wallet password, written 0600 by airgap_tx_signer because a password on
# argv is world-readable via /proc/<pid>/cmdline. Deleted in a finally; a
# SIGKILL leaves it, and it must never be committed if it does.
.gs_pw_*

# Wallet output-set export written by airgap_tx_signer phase_create so the
# offline wallet can sign spends of earlier rounds. Maps the wallet holdings.
outputs_export.hex

# The Pi/vault wake channel. The .key files hold an X25519 SECRET each; the
# state file is the job ledger; the handles file maps a handle to the bundle
# and slip it names. Suffixed patterns, NOT "gs_wake_*" -- that would shadow
# the tracked scripts gs_wake_keys, gs_wake_agent and gs_wake_proto.py.
gs_wake_*.key
gs_wake_state.json
gs_wake_handles.json
# receive_watch --result-json's outcome, written into the same artifact_dir as
# the two above by the wake agent's swap_status job. It carries `unlocked` and
# `total` as exact decimals -- how much of the swap has arrived, to the
# piconero. It was in neither this file nor the wipe list, and it is the fourth
# of four files gs_wake_agent writes to that directory; the other three were in
# both. tests/test_gitignore.py could not catch it, because it enforces
# "everything the wipe erases is ignored" and this was in NEITHER list.
gs_wake_status.json
.gs_wake_inhibit
# A woken job's children write here instead of to the systemd journal. It holds
# whatever thor_swap_preparer printed, which includes the BTC deposit address
# and the ThorChain memo -- and the memo names the destination XMR address.
gs_wake_job.log
# integrity_log_once's run-scoped dedupe marker. It holds one line per
# chain event kind -- redacted now, but still the run's event vocabulary,
# and it is written next to the plans.
.chain_once_*
pager_state.json
pager.log
